-- title:
--   Regularity of the pole chart of X_H(q²M') at ∞
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carries $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((\mathsf q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $q^2M'$ and subgroup $H=\ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that field of $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $\mathsf q$-expansions. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of $\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ`, the $\mathsf q$-expansion of the $j$-invariant. Write $A_\infty$ for `chartAlgInf A K j`, the integral closure of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, and let $\mathfrak n\subseteq A_\infty$ be a prime ideal consisting exactly of those $b$ whose $\mathsf q$-expansion has $\mathsf q^0$-coefficient in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$. Then for any ring $B$ that is a localisation of $A_\infty$ at $\mathfrak n$: $B$ is a regular local ring, $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} B=2$, the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak n$ in $B$ is generated by the images of $\varpi$ and of $j^{-1}$, and $B/\varpi B$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the regularity of the two-chart integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ over $A$ at the $\mathsf q$-adic cusp $\infty$ of the special fibre: the local ring there is two-dimensional regular with regular parameters $\varpi$ and $1/j$, and the fibre over $\varpi$ is again regular. It feeds the statement about the special fibre at primes of the pole chart cut out by Gauss-type conditions, used in the study of the reduction of $X_H$ at $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty_xH.lean

